=====Usage notes=====
* {{m|zh||A[[除以]]B}} means "A divided by B". {{m|zh||A除B}} means "B divided by A", but in colloquial speech is the same as {{m|zh||A除以B}}.
** {{m|zh||除}} is a transitive verb, and {{m|zh||A除B}} is understood as {{m|zh||用A除B}} or {{m|zh||以A除B|lit=to divide B by A}}, the latter of which is attested in Literary Chinese and likely gave rise to {{m|zh|除以}}. This contrasts with {{m|zh|減}}, which is an intransitive verb and {{m|zh||A減B}} means "A decreases by B", i.e. "A minus B".

