{{ja-accent-dialectal|region=Keihan|t|あ|め|ぇ|àmě}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|あめ}}

# [[rain]], [[rainfall]]
#: {{ja-uxi|'''雨'''が降っている。|'''^あめ''' が ふって いる。|It's raining.|lit='''Rain''' is falling.}}
# a [[rainy]] [[weather]]
#: {{syn|ja|雨天|tr=uten}}
# {{lb|ja|sort=あめ|figurative}} something [[fall#Verb|falling]] like rain
# {{senseid|ja|hanafuda}}{{lb|ja|sort=あめ|hanafuda}} The [[willow]] or rain [[suit]] in a [[hanafuda]] [[deck]], representing the month of [[November]] and the number [[eleven]] in most of Japan ([[June]] and [[six]] in {{m|ja|虫花|tr=mushibana}} decks, [[February]] and [[two]] in games from the [[Nagoya]] region, and [[December]] and [[twelve]] in [[Korea]])
#: {{syn|ja|柳|tr1=yanagi|t1=willow|id1=hanafuda}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In most cases, ''ame'' becomes ''same'' when it serves as the latter element of a compound. It is unclear if this leading {{IPAchar|/s/}} is indicative of an earlier ''same'', or if this was an {{w|epenthesis}} for [[euphony]] to avoid vowel clusters, or for other reasons. This {{IPAchar|/s/}} is also seen in {{m|ja|青|tr=ao|pos=becoming ''sao'' in old compounds}} and {{m|ja|稲|tr=ine|pos=becoming ''shine'' in old compounds}}. Given that this {{IPAchar|/s/}} only ever appears interstitially, and given the semantics, this {{IPAchar|/s/}} may be cognate with {{cog|ko|-}} interfix {{m|ko|-ㅅ-|-ᄉ-|tr=-s-}} used to mark possession, much like {{cog|en|-s-}}.

